WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.500 --> 00:00:10.000
Bigwala Cultural Group performing "Wandyaku Vooto"
Bukoona Village, Busoga Kingdom, Uganda

2
00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:25.000
[Bigwala — a royal music tradition performed with
gourd trumpets blown in hocket to produce melody]

3
00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:45.000
[Each trumpet sounds a single note — the musicians
interlock their rhythms to build a collective voice]

4
00:00:46.000 --> 00:01:10.000
[The performance begins with a single trumpet,
then others join, followed by drummers, singers, and dancers]

5
00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:35.000
[Song lyrics narrate the history of the Basoga people
and the legacy of their kings]

6
00:01:36.000 --> 00:02:05.000
[Bigwala historically marked royal occasions —
coronations, funerals, and ceremonies of state]

7
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:35.000
[Performers move in circular formations around five drummers,
swaying gently and raising their hands in rhythm]

8
00:02:36.000 --> 00:03:05.000
[Only four elderly masters still possess the knowledge
to craft the gourd trumpets and teach the tradition]

9
00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:35.000
[UNESCO inscribed Bigwala on the Urgent Safeguarding List —
recognizing the immediate threat to its survival]

10
00:03:36.000 --> 00:04:05.000
[The Bigwala Cultural Group preserves what remains,
passing rhythm and memory to the next generation]

11
00:04:06.000 --> 00:04:38.000
[A sound from the Busoga Kingdom —
still played, still carried forward]
